[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Kulshan: Hardware architecture trade study
UID: KUL-ARC
VERSION: 1.0
PREFIX: KUL-ARC-
METADATA:
  AUTHOR: Ben Tyrrell-Davis
  Ben: Engineer

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: trade_study.sgra

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose and Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This trade study selects the high level hardware architecture for the Kulshan sports watch.

**Decision to be made:** which hardware architecture to baseline for the watch.

**Out of scope:** User interfaces, system software architecture, mechanical design decisions (though there may be mechanical requirements that influence the trade)

**Method:** Each alternative is first screened against Gate criteria (pass/fail).
Alternatives that pass all gates are scored 1-5 against each Weighted criterion.
The weighted score is the sum of (weight x score) divided by the total weight.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Evaluation Criteria

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-3
CRITERION_TYPE: Weighted
CATEGORY: Performance
WEIGHT: 1
TITLE: HRM accuracy and measurement capability
STATEMENT: >>>
The degree to which the system can provide accurate HRM.
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* 5: Equivalent accuracy to ECG.
* 3: Meets and exceeds MOE-001-003.
* 1: Doesn't meet MOE-001-003, or some part of it.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-003
  ROLE: Derived from

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-4
CRITERION_TYPE: Weighted
CATEGORY: Schedule
WEIGHT: 1
TITLE: HRM accuracy and cost of development time
STATEMENT: >>>
Complexity of the HRM algorithm, pertaining to how much time it will take to develop the algorithm.
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* 5: Development of the algorithm is not a concern and will take very little time.
* 3: Development of the algorithm is not a concern for schedule, but will take moderate effort.
* 1: Development of the algorithm will take most of the available schedule.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-003
  ROLE: Derived from

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-9
CRITERION_TYPE: Weighted
CATEGORY: Performance
WEIGHT: 1
TITLE: SPO2 accuracy and measurement capability
STATEMENT: >>>
The degree to which the system can provide accurate SPO2 data
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* 5: Very accurate SPO2 data
* 3: Good SPO2 data
* 1: Poor SPO2 data
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-011
  ROLE: Derived from

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-8
CRITERION_TYPE: Weighted
CATEGORY: Schedule
WEIGHT: 1
TITLE: SPO2 accuracy and cost of development time
STATEMENT: >>>
Complexity of the SPO2 algorithm, pertaining to how much time it will take to develop the algorithm.
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* 5: Low cost of development.
* 3: Medium cost of development.
* 1: High cost of development.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-011
  ROLE: Derived from

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-2
CRITERION_TYPE: Gate
CATEGORY: Performance
WEIGHT: N/A
TITLE: Bluetooth classic streaming
STATEMENT: >>>
The system supports bluetooth classic streaming to slave device.
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* Pass: System does support bluetooth classic streaming to one or more slave devices.
* Fail: System does not support bluetooth classic streaming to any slave devices.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Directly required by MOE-001-002. The system cannot satisfy system requirements regardless of other merits.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-002
  ROLE: Derived from

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-5
CRITERION_TYPE: Weighted
CATEGORY: Performance
WEIGHT: 1
TITLE: Wireless connectivity
STATEMENT: >>>
The degree to which the system is compatible with wireless data transfer
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* 5: System is very flexible and has many methods for wireless connectivity
* 3: System is moderately flexible, and meets the requirements.
* 1: System meets the requirements, just barely.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
MOE-001-004 directly specifies that the device should not have a method of physically  connecting the device to a computer. The device must then have a method to connect to the outside world.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-004
  ROLE: Derived from

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-6
CRITERION_TYPE: Weighted
CATEGORY: Performance
WEIGHT: 1
TITLE: Charge time
STATEMENT: >>>
The degree to which the system supports fast charging
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* 5: The system with the fastest charge time.
* 3: The system with the 2nd fastest charge time.
* 1: The system with the slowest charge time.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-006
  ROLE: Derived from

[CRITERION]
UID: CR-7
CRITERION_TYPE: Weighted
CATEGORY: Cost
WEIGHT: 1
TITLE: BoM Cost
STATEMENT: >>>
Total production cost of the system
<<<
SCORING_GUIDE: >>>
* 5: Cost is lowest
* 3: Cost is moderate
* 1: Cost is highest
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
MOE-001-007 specifies that the BoM cost is less than $250
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MOE-001-007
  ROLE: Derived from

